                <pb facs="0189" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg85"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 150.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Commander Reiter, U. S. S. Ranger, to Mr.
                    Mizner</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José de Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-08-27"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 27,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[Received in telegraph office, Guatemala, at 8 p.m.; received
                    at legation at 10 p.m.]</p>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mizner</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">United States Minister:</hi></p>
                <p>Barrundia expected in steamer. As peace is declared, I suggest that you ask
                    Government to permit <hi rendition="#italic">Thetis</hi> to take him to
                    Acapulco, we acknowledging their municipal rights over steamer. Steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Acapulco</hi> in sight.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reiter.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
